# R session cruft
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
Rplots.pdf

# Generated basemaps live on a local drive outside the repo (cfg$out_root in
# make_WFS_basemaps.R). Nothing generated should be committed here.
output/
*.asc
*.prj
*.aux.xml
*.log
*.png

# ...except the README figures, which are checked in deliberately.
!docs/img/*.png

# Source data. The whole tree is excluded, then three small folders are added
# back because they are either irreplaceable or awkward to re-source:
#   regions/          age0_survey_regions_5min_mod.asc is HAND-EDITED and exists
#                     nowhere else; the age-0 shapefile came from a Python
#                     digitizing step that is not reproducible in R
#   management_areas/ 8 small zips that are the definition of the areas
#   ports/            a specific FWC ReportCreator query (1985-2025, all
#                     species) that would have to be reconstructed exactly
#
# Still excluded, deliberately:
#   seagrass/         Seagrass_Statewide.shp alone is 230 MB, over GitHub's
#                     100 MB per-file hard limit
#   *.gdb/            275 MB, and FWRI-supplied - check redistribution terms
#   dbseabed/         downloads itself via fn.pull_dbseabed()
#   artificial_reefs/ source is marked REDACTED; check terms before publishing
data/*
!data/management_areas/
!data/ports/
!data/regions/

# The extension rules above still apply inside those folders, so undo them
# where the region inputs need to survive.
!data/regions/*.asc
!data/regions/*.prj
